WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.940
Every captain keeps a log,

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.020
because a ship without one forgets.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.040
It forgets which channels were shallow,

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.250
and every mistake gets made again.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.570
That's how most agent sessions begin:

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:15.620
with amnesia.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.200
The agent doesn't know what was built

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:17.680
yesterday,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.840
or which three approaches to a problem

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.090
were tried last week.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.460
Picture an hour -long session.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.700
The agent tries two approaches that fail,

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.230
discovers a quirk in the database driver,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.700
and lands a clean solution.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.180
The code is committed,

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.920
but the knowledge lived in the context

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.440
window,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.230
and now it's gone.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.520
Tomorrow's session will cheerfully try the same

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.710
two dead ends.

00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:41.607
The usual tools only go so far.

00:00:41.697 --> 00:00:43.857
Instruction files hold stable knowledge,

00:00:43.857 --> 00:00:45.717
but nobody updates them for every small

00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:46.567
discovery.

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:49.087
Git history records what changed,

00:00:49.097 --> 00:00:50.287
not what was learned.

00:00:50.577 --> 00:00:52.737
And session summaries only work if someone

00:00:52.737 --> 00:00:53.897
remembers to write them,

00:00:53.897 --> 00:00:55.827
at the end of a long day.

00:00:56.584 --> 00:00:58.024
The fix is active memory:

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.984
a system that captures knowledge as it's

00:00:59.984 --> 00:01:00.664
created,

00:01:00.664 --> 00:01:01.584
organizes it,

00:01:01.584 --> 00:01:03.294
and serves it back when it's needed.

00:01:03.404 --> 00:01:05.784
Knowledge now flows from every past session

00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:06.924
into the current one,

00:01:06.924 --> 00:01:08.824
including sessions run by teammates,

00:01:08.824 --> 00:01:09.864
weeks ago.

00:01:09.864 --> 00:01:11.494
A note in the log reads:

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.864
shoal at low tide,

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:13.824
stay east.

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:16.004
That lesson cost someone a damaged ship.

00:01:16.004 --> 00:01:17.924
The log makes sure it only costs

00:01:17.924 --> 00:01:18.774
one.

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:20.909
Structure makes it searchable.

00:01:20.919 --> 00:01:22.409
Wings for projects,

00:01:22.419 --> 00:01:23.699
rooms for topics,

00:01:23.699 --> 00:01:25.859
and drawers that hold verbatim records,

00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:26.949
not summaries.

00:01:26.959 --> 00:01:28.409
At the start of a session,

00:01:28.419 --> 00:01:29.949
the agent loads what's known.

00:01:30.079 --> 00:01:30.719
During it,

00:01:30.719 --> 00:01:32.489
the agent stores its discoveries.

00:01:32.639 --> 00:01:33.619
At the end,

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:35.189
a hook saves the work automatically.

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:38.428
Share the store and agents working in

00:01:38.428 --> 00:01:40.318
parallel stop working blind.

00:01:40.408 --> 00:01:42.828
One agent finds a missing database index

00:01:42.828 --> 00:01:44.028
and writes it down.

00:01:44.028 --> 00:01:44.928
Another agent,

00:01:44.928 --> 00:01:46.138
building the front end,

00:01:46.148 --> 00:01:48.178
reads that note before it starts.

00:01:48.348 --> 00:01:50.688
Each agent keeps its own diary and

00:01:50.688 --> 00:01:52.198
everyone can read them all.

00:01:52.897 --> 00:01:53.797
Be choosy.

00:01:53.797 --> 00:01:55.977
Store what's expensive to rediscover:

00:01:55.977 --> 00:01:57.487
undocumented behavior,

00:01:57.497 --> 00:01:59.257
decisions and their reasons,

00:01:59.257 --> 00:02:00.667
approaches that failed.

00:02:00.797 --> 00:02:02.657
Skip what the code already says.

00:02:02.657 --> 00:02:05.127
And treat memory as an attack surface.

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:07.297
A poisoned note doesn't vanish when the

00:02:07.297 --> 00:02:08.077
session ends.

00:02:08.077 --> 00:02:09.527
It comes back next week.

00:02:10.223 --> 00:02:11.683
When a note keeps coming up,

00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.943
promote it into a convention,

00:02:12.943 --> 00:02:14.103
or a test.

00:02:14.103 --> 00:02:15.543
Your agents are the crew,

00:02:15.543 --> 00:02:17.073
and every crew is temporary.

00:02:17.263 --> 00:02:18.723
The log is what lets the next

00:02:18.723 --> 00:02:20.473
voyage start from understanding.

00:02:20.623 --> 00:02:21.563
Next up:

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:23.153
extending the agent's reach.
